{% from "_macros.html.j2" import means, does_not_show with context %}
{% set B = iv.q5 %}
{% set n = q5.home.NHL %}
<p class="close-kicker">Question 5 · Czech hockey atlas · {{ q5.window }}</p>
<h1 class="slide-q">{{ cur.title }}</h1>
<p class="slide-a">Over {{ q5.window }}, the median Czech NHL skater played <strong>{{ f2(n.median_toi_ratio) }} times</strong> the median ice time of his league, season and position (95 % bootstrap interval by player {{ f2(B.NHL.toi.lo) }}–{{ f2(B.NHL.toi.hi) }}) and scored {{ f2(n.median_ppg_ratio) }} times its points per game ({{ f2(B.NHL.ppg.lo) }}–{{ f2(B.NHL.ppg.hi) }}; {{ n.players }} players, {{ n.player_seasons }} player-seasons).</p>
<figure class="figure-bleed" data-chart="q5-abroad">
  <table class="fig-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">League</th><th scope="col" class="num">Czech players</th><th scope="col" class="num">player-seasons</th><th scope="col" class="num">ice time ÷ median (95 % bootstrap interval)</th><th scope="col" class="num">points per game ÷ median (95 % bootstrap interval)</th><th scope="col" class="num">share above the median, ice time / points</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{% for lg, v in q5.home.items() %}<tr><td>{{ lg }}</td><td class="num">{{ v.players }}</td><td class="num">{{ v.player_seasons }}</td><td class="num">{{ f2(v.median_toi_ratio) }} ({{ f2(B[lg].toi.lo) }}–{{ f2(B[lg].toi.hi) }})</td><td class="num">{{ f2(v.median_ppg_ratio) }} ({{ f2(B[lg].ppg.lo) }}–{{ f2(B[lg].ppg.hi) }})</td><td class="num">{{ pct0(v.share_above_median_toi) }} / {{ pct0(v.share_above_median_ppg) }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
  </table>
  <figcaption><strong>Figure 1.</strong> Median ratio of a nation's qualifying skaters to the league-season median at the same position, {{ q5.window }}, by league (1.0 = the median). How to read it: Czechia is the blue dot; filled ink dots are peers with ten or more player-seasons in that league, hollow ones fewer. Switch between ice time and points per game. The intervals in the table resample Czech players, with all of a player's seasons kept together. {% if q5.own_below_one %}A league's own players (Finns in the Liiga, Swedes in the SHL) sit below 1.0 because they make up most of each roster, depth players included, and imported players are compared with them.{% endif %}</figcaption>
</figure>
<section class="q-evidence" aria-labelledby="q5-evidence">
  <h2 class="q-sub" id="q5-evidence">Evidence</h2>
  <p class="slide-did"><span class="slide-did-label">What was counted</span> Qualifying skaters (the games threshold) over {{ q5.window }}; each player-season is divided by the median of all qualifying skaters of the same league, season and position (forward or defenceman), and the table shows the median of those ratios. {{ q5.n_player_seasons }} Czech player-seasons in all; {{ q5.unknown_position }} have no position and are left out. Only players who reached the threshold are included, so players who went abroad and did not reach it are not in the ratios.</p>
  <p class="slide-how"><span class="slide-how-label">By position</span> NHL forwards ({{ B.NHL_by_position.F.toi.clusters }} players): {{ f2(q5.by_position.NHL.F.median_toi_ratio) }} on ice time ({{ f2(B.NHL_by_position.F.toi.lo) }}–{{ f2(B.NHL_by_position.F.toi.hi) }}) and {{ f2(q5.by_position.NHL.F.median_ppg_ratio) }} on points ({{ f2(B.NHL_by_position.F.ppg.lo) }}–{{ f2(B.NHL_by_position.F.ppg.hi) }}). NHL defencemen ({{ B.NHL_by_position.D.toi.clusters }} players): {{ f2(q5.by_position.NHL.D.median_toi_ratio) }} ({{ f2(B.NHL_by_position.D.toi.lo) }}–{{ f2(B.NHL_by_position.D.toi.hi) }}) and {{ f2(q5.by_position.NHL.D.median_ppg_ratio) }} ({{ f2(B.NHL_by_position.D.ppg.lo) }}–{{ f2(B.NHL_by_position.D.ppg.hi) }}). The NHL figure for all skaters mixes these two groups, so the share of defencemen moves it. Liiga forwards {{ f2(q5.by_position.Liiga.F.median_ppg_ratio) }} on points, SHL forwards {{ f2(q5.by_position.SHL.F.median_ppg_ratio) }}.</p>
</section>
{% call means() %}
<p>In the NHL, the median Czech skater's ice time and scoring are close to the league median for his position{% if B.NHL.toi.lo < 1 < B.NHL.toi.hi and B.NHL.ppg.lo < 1 < B.NHL.ppg.hi %}, and both intervals include 1{% endif %}. In the Liiga and the SHL the Czech median ratios are above 1{% if B.SHL.toi.lo < 1 or B.SHL.ppg.lo < 1 %} (the SHL intervals reach below 1){% endif %}, but there Czech players are imports compared with each league's own depth players, so the ratios are not comparable across leagues and are not adjusted for league strength. The ratios describe the players who reached the threshold abroad; they do not show how Czech players who stayed at home, or who did not reach the threshold, would have fared.</p>
{% endcall %}
{% call does_not_show() %}
<li>A league-quality adjustment: a ratio of 1.3 in the SHL is not a better result than 1.0 in the NHL.</li>
<li>Players who did not reach the games threshold abroad (selection).</li>
{% endcall %}
